.TH sane-scansnap 5 "11 Oct 2026" "SANE Scanner Access Now Easy" "Scanner Access Now Easy"
.SH NAME
sane-scansnap \- SANE backend for ScanSnap network scanners
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B sane-scansnap
library implements a SANE backend for the PFU ScanSnap iX1300 using its local
Wi-Fi protocol.  The current implementation supports 300 dpi color, grayscale, and black-and-white scanning,
simplex and duplex acquisition, automatic document length, and automatic page
cropping.
.PP
The ADF and return/card feed are exported as separate logical devices.  This
allows frontends which only understand generic feeder and duplex sources to
select either physical path.
.SH SCAN MODES
The mode option accepts Color (24-bit RGB), Gray (8-bit grayscale), and
Lineart (1-bit black-and-white). All modes acquire a color JPEG from the
scanner. Gray decodes its luminance on the host; Lineart applies a fixed
threshold of 128, with darker pixels rendered black. These output modes do
not reduce network traffic. Both feed paths support all three modes in
simplex and duplex operation.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The configuration file is
.IR @CONFIGDIR@/scansnap.conf .
Add one line for each scanner, using a stable IPv4 address:
.PP
.RS
.B net 192.168.0.145
.RE
.PP
The scanner and host must be on the same local network.  A fixed address
should be reserved in DHCP.  Alternatively, search the local networks each
time the backend starts, so the scanner is found at whatever address it has:
.PP
.RS
.B net auto
.RE
.PP
The search broadcasts on every local network and lists each scanner that
answers.  Replies arrive on UDP port 55274, which a host firewall must allow
from the local network; a fixed address needs no firewall rule.
.PP
The following settings apply to every configured scanner, wherever they
appear in the file:
.TP
.BR "rotate adf" | return " 0" | 180
Rotate every page scanned through that feed path by 180 degrees.  Use
.B 180
when sheets are loaded bottom edge first, for example with the text upright
and facing you in the ADF paper chute.  The default,
.BR 0 ,
matches sheets loaded top edge first as the scanner manual describes.  The
.B rotate
option overrides this for a single scan, for example
.BR "scanimage \-\-rotate=no" .
.TP
.BR return-path " yes" | no
With
.BR no ,
only the ADF device is listed and the Return Path device is hidden.  The
default is
.BR yes .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I @CONFIGDIR@/scansnap.conf
Backend configuration file.
.TP
.I @LIBDIR@/libsane-scansnap.a
Static library implementing this backend.
.TP
.I @LIBDIR@/libsane-scansnap.so
Shared library implementing this backend.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SANE_DEBUG_SCANSNAP
Controls backend debug output.  Higher values increase verbosity.
.SH LIMITATIONS
Only the ScanSnap iX1300 Wi-Fi transport is currently supported.  USB,
native scanner grayscale/monochrome commands, other resolutions, encrypted
protocol mode, and scanner
configuration are not implemented yet.  Deskew, OCR, page editing, and PDF
creation are expected to be performed by the SANE frontend.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sane (7),
.BR scanimage (1)
